sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, R1-R4, decision swamp-vault-secrets (vault.get), orbit-gateway-renders-create-env (Gateway owns .env, no read-back), DECISIONS instance.sync_environment (vault after commit, @swamp/ssh from 209, no private-material fetch, no per-Node worker). docs/reference/environment-variables.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: env:sync
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: env:sync --instance=42<br/>--json
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit env:sync --instance=42`
  %%> - syntax: `env:sync --instance=SELECTOR [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance: a numeric Instance ID or the exact domain of its Route
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, render .env<br/>Instance 42 · task #5131
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, the Node of Instance 42
  %%> - Instance 42 is active, on a Node with exactly one active `app-dev` or `app-prod` role
  %%> - Instance 42 has stored configuration (`env.configuration_missing` otherwise)
  %%> - a stored `{{instance.domain}}` needs a settled Route (`env.reference_unavailable` otherwise)
  %%> - no other task holds Instance 42; the Gateway holds one lock per Instance and waits briefly for a busy one
  %%> Renders .env:
  %%> - every stored key in sorted order, as a quoted value
  %%> - `{{instance.domain}}` from the Route, `{{instance.environment}}` from the Node role
  %%> - `.env.testing` too, when Instance 42 owns its `DB` database
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5131 recorded with the full intent and the sha256 of each rendered file
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Push .env to the vault<br/>vault: env-5131, env-testing-5131
  %%> Why:
  %%> - `.env` holds secrets, which travel only through the vault (R3)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - after the task commits, pushes the rendered files into Swamp's vault on Node 209
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the run reads them with `vault.get`; no step calls the Gateway back
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-environment
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the account, the application directory, the file paths and the expected sha256 of each file
  %%> - the key names Orbit wrote last time, which it may remove
  %%> - production only: the release path and the Processes with `restart_on_deploy`
  %%> - secrets only as vault key names
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5131
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check for foreign keys<br/>@swamp/ssh · key names only
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the account, the path, the file type and owner, without following a link
  %%> - compares the key names of the current `.env` with the stored keys and the keys Orbit wrote last time
  %%> - a missing file is fine
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a key that only the file holds would be lost; the step refuses instead (`env.sync_would_drop_keys`)
  %%> Not returned:
  %%> - no value leaves the Node; only the names of foreign keys, on failure
  SW->>N: Write .env, .env.testing<br/>vault.get · temp file, rename
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered `.env` from the vault to a temporary file with mode `0600`, owned by the Instance account, then renames it over `.env`
  %%> - writes `.env.testing` the same way, unless Git tracks it in the checkout
  %%> - leaves a file that already matches in place
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - the Instance account named in the intent, not root
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - renders nothing; the Gateway already rendered the files
  SW->>N: Check the written file<br/>sha256 = rendered sha256
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - compares the sha256 of each file on the Node with the sha256 in the intent
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the sync only counts when the Node holds exactly what the Gateway rendered
  %%> - this replaces `env.sync_unconfirmed`: a rerun checks and writes again
  opt production Instance
    SW->>N: Refresh the runtime<br/>config:cache · OPcache · Processes
    %%> When:
    %%> - on every production sync, also when `.env` did not change
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - rebuilds an existing config cache in a temporary path, checks it, then replaces the old one; an uncached release stays uncached
    %%> - reloads the PHP-FPM pool to reset OPcache
    %%> - restarts the running Processes that have `restart_on_deploy`
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - development Instances: they only get the file
  end
  alt every file matches
    N-->>SW: files match, refreshed
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - whether each file changed, and the runtime refresh status
    %%> Not returned:
    %%> - no values and no file content
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · changed flags
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run's outputs; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>owned keys · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the synced key names become the keys Orbit owns on Instance 42
    %%> - task #5131 succeeds with `changed`, the testing status and the refresh status
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or foreign keys
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, the file is unsafe, a foreign key would drop, or a hash does not match
    %%> - production: the config cache or the Process restart fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, for example `env.sync_would_drop_keys` with the key names
    Note over GW: Keep stored values<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - stored values and the owned-key list stay as they were
    %%> - task #5131 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a refused file stays unchanged; a failed cache build keeps the old cache
    %%> - a file already written stays; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause, for example store or remove the foreign keys, then run `env:sync` again; it is a new task
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5131
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
